    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "tb-conflict-definition",
        "moduleId": "conflict-origin",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "教材定义：什么情况算冲突",
        "markdown": "教材把合并冲突定义为一种**行级判断的分歧**：当同一行内容在两个独立分支中被以不同方式修改，或者一个文件在其中一个分支里被删除、却在另一个分支里被编辑时，冲突就发生了。\n\n改动互不重叠时，Git 可以平稳地自动合并；一旦出现上述分歧，自动合并就会失败，把决定权交回给开发者。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-dacd3293b5aedfe0e5a195bd",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000031"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Going Further with Git",
                "Handling Conflicts"
              ],
              "lineStart": 2947,
              "lineEnd": 3217,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "b512f51c9d7d5cbfc23177a89c5aabc27a313169b4bd46345d29ba2a107c7da7"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-conflict-intuition",
        "moduleId": "conflict-origin",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "补充：冲突不是错误",
        "markdown": "可以这样理解：合并时 Git 要为每个位置决定「取哪一边」。只被一边改过的行，答案唯一；两边都改过且改法不同的行，Git 没有足够信息判断谁才是想要的，于是停下来等人裁决。\n\n所以冲突不是 Git 崩溃，也不是文件被损坏，而是 Git 拒绝替你做业务判断。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-conflict-definition"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-conflict-scenario",
        "moduleId": "conflict-origin",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "教材例子：同一个 README 被两边改",
        "markdown": "教材用一个具体例子演示冲突的诞生：在 `master` 上给 `README.md` 添加贡献者列表并提交；新建 `docs` 分支，用同一文件的同一位置补充项目简介并提交；再切回 `master` 合并 `docs` 时，Git 报告：\n\n```text\nAuto-merging README.md\nCONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in README.md\nAutomatic merge failed; fix conflicts and then commit the result.\n```\n\n两处改动落在同一文件的同一区域，Git 无法确定它们最终该以什么形式共存。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-dacd3293b5aedfe0e5a195bd",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000031"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Going Further with Git",
                "Handling Conflicts"
              ],
              "lineStart": 2947,
              "lineEnd": 3217,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "b512f51c9d7d5cbfc23177a89c5aabc27a313169b4bd46345d29ba2a107c7da7"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-merge-logic",
        "moduleId": "conflict-origin",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "title": "补充：Git 为什么把两边都留下",
        "markdown": "Git 并不会丢掉任何一边，它把两边的候选内容都保留在文件里，只是加上标记说明来源。原因是它比较两个分支的最新提交与它们的共同祖先，能发现两边都动了同一块区域，却无法判断「贡献者列表」和「项目简介」应该以什么顺序组合——那是内容决策，不是算法能推断的事实。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-conflict-definition",
            "tb-conflict-scenario"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-conflict-markers",
        "moduleId": "marker-anatomy",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "title": "教材：冲突标记的结构",
        "markdown": "进入冲突文件后，Git 用一组固定标记把两边的候选内容分开：\n\n```text\n<<<<<<< HEAD\n## Contributors\n\n- Amira Khan <amira@zipf.org>\n=======\nThese Zipf's Law scripts tally occurrences of words in text\nfiles and plot each word's rank versus its frequency.\n>>>>>>> docs\n```\n\n从 `<<<<<<< HEAD` 到 `=======` 之间是当前分支（此处为 `master`）的内容；从 `=======` 到 `>>>>>>> docs` 之间是被合并分支 `docs` 的内容。同一个文件里若有多处冲突区域，Git 会为每一处都放一组这样的标记。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-dacd3293b5aedfe0e5a195bd",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000031"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Going Further with Git",
                "Handling Conflicts"
              ],
              "lineStart": 2947,
              "lineEnd": 3217,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "b512f51c9d7d5cbfc23177a89c5aabc27a313169b4bd46345d29ba2a107c7da7"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-marker-reading",
        "moduleId": "marker-anatomy",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "补充：三步读懂一组标记",
        "markdown": "读标记的顺序可以固定下来：\n\n1. 看 `<<<<<<<` 后面的名字，确定当前所在分支（`HEAD` 指向它）；\n2. `=======` 是两侧内容的分界线；\n3. `>>>>>>>` 后面的名字是被合并进来的分支。\n\n把这三行当作临时脚手架：它们本身不是文件内容，最终必须从文件中消失。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-conflict-markers"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-resolution-options",
        "moduleId": "resolution-steps",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "procedure",
        "title": "教材：四种处理选择",
        "markdown": "教材列出解决冲突时的四种选择：保留 `master` 的改动、保留 `docs` 的改动、编辑这一段把两边合并，或者写出全新的内容。不论选择哪一种，都必须删除 `>>>`、`===` 和 `<<<` 这些标记。\n\n本例选择合并两边：先保留项目简介，再列出贡献者。决定完成后，文件里不再有任何冲突标记。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-dacd3293b5aedfe0e5a195bd",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000031"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Going Further with Git",
                "Handling Conflicts"
              ],
              "lineStart": 2947,
              "lineEnd": 3217,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "b512f51c9d7d5cbfc23177a89c5aabc27a313169b4bd46345d29ba2a107c7da7"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-resolution-steps",
        "moduleId": "resolution-steps",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "procedure",
        "title": "补充：可复用的解决步骤",
        "markdown": "把教材的做法整理成固定步骤：\n\n1. 用 `git status` 找出处于未合并状态的文件；\n2. 打开每个冲突文件，逐处阅读标记；\n3. 为每一处决定保留哪一侧、合并两侧，还是重写；\n4. 删除所有 `<<<<<<<`、`=======`、`>>>>>>>` 行，并把内容改成最终形态；\n5. 用 `git add <文件>` 把已解决的内容放入暂存区；\n6. 用 `git commit` 完成合并提交。\n\n如果提交前仍有标记残留，说明还有冲突没处理完，此时不要提交。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-resolution-options"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-commit-resolution",
        "moduleId": "resolution-steps",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "procedure",
        "title": "教材：像普通编辑一样提交",
        "markdown": "解决冲突后的处理与普通编辑一致：先 `git add README.md` 把内容加入暂存区，再 `git commit -m \"Merging README additions\"` 完成合并提交。\n\n提交后，`git log --oneline -n 4` 仍显示一条线性历史；只有加上 `--graph` 才能看到真实的合并结构：\n\n```text\n*   55c63d0 (HEAD -> master) Merging README additions\n|\\\n| * a0b88e5 (docs) Added repository overview\n* | 45a576b Added contributor list\n|/\n* 232b564 Initial commit of README file\n```\n\n合并提交把两条分支历史连接成一个整体。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
